---A `ParamType` config provides a way to retrieve named data from other data structures.
---
---Params do not contain the value itself, only the default value to return when a data structure does not contain a
---value for that param.
---
---For example, ObjType configs for armour items may contain data for `config.Param.DEFEND_SOUND_1`, with each config
---returning a different sound ID value to play.
---
---Data structures that contain params, or provide methods using params, are:
---
---These config types can be found within the `config.Param` table:
---
---Info: An `ParamType` is a Proxy usertype, which means it is safe to copy and store in your scripts. It cannot,
---however, be used with any persistent storage.
---
---Information available within an `ParamType` includes:
---@class ParamType
---@field id integer (Read-only) The ID of this config type.
---@field configName string (Read-only) The name of this config, i.e. `"DEFEND_SOUND_1"`.
---@field typeName string (Read-only) The type of this config. Will always be `"Param"`.
---@field valueType ValueType (Read-only) The expected type of data this param will return.
---@field defaultValue any (Read-only) Returns the default value of this param config. The value data type ValueType is provided by `valueType`. If the param does not exist within the data structure being used, this is the value which will be returned.
